# Optional, for z20 backlight (install.sh asks): the logged-in user may give the Z20 a keyboard light
# of its own, an LED through the kernel's uleds (loaded at boot: modules-load.d/evga-z20.conf), which
# UPower then offers. Without this rule z20 backlight works all the same, without the LED.
# It lets any program in the desktop session add LEDs; it can't change other LEDs.
# 70-, as 70-evga-z20.rules: uaccess has to be tagged before 73-seat-late.rules.
KERNEL=="uleds", SUBSYSTEM=="misc", TAG+="uaccess"
